WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.750
We were consumed by bloodlust.

3
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:08.790
The Shandorian Warriors.

4
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.960
They only attacked
God's Island, Upper Yard,

5
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:15.050
because they wanted to regain
the homeland of their ancestors,

6
00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:16.430
which we took.

7
00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:17.930
[squawks]

8
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.970
[PRIEST A]
My Lord, you're
not thinking about that again,

9
00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.560
are you? Look around.

10
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.910
Look at the peaceful existence
of the citizens of Skypiea.

11
00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:28.200
It wouldn't be this way had
our ancestors not taken control

12
00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:31.080
of the Upper Yard 400 years ago.

13
00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:32.530
And it is our duty

14
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:36.030
to carry on this battle to
ensure the peaceful nature

15
00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:37.820
of this nation.

16
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.220
We've tried to
negotiate with them.

17
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.720
But if they cannot abide
by these negotiations,

18
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.650
they do not deserve
your compassion.

19
00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:52.240
[GAN FALL]
Four hundred years.

20
00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.820
I think that it's time for this

21
00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.700
endless strife and bloodshed
to come to an end.

22
00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.410
I only wish that we could
all live in harmony.

23
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.710
And put these needless
battles behind us.

24
00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:11.130
[PRIEST B]
Enemy attack! Enemy attack!

25
00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:14.680
[PRIEST A]
Is it another attack
by the Shandorians?

26
00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.210
[PRIEST B]
It's not them.

27
00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.330
[PRIEST A]
What do you mean?

28
00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.390
It's a man who calls
himself God Eneru.

29
00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.630
What? God Eneru?

30
00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:18.760
<b>Quintet</b>

31
00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.630
[SUU]
Suu.

32
00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:21.640
[CONIS]
I want you to stay and
take care of these two, Suu.

33
00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.510
Because there's something
important I have to do.

34
00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:31.770
[CONIS]
I have to warn them,
no matter what it takes.

35
00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:35.000
I won't let your death
be in vain, Father.

36
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.340
[CONIS]
I can't.

37
00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:38.050
I can't just sit here and cry.

38
00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:41.220
[CHILDREN laughing]

39
00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:42.330
[CHILD B]
Here!

40
00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.890
Hey!

41
00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.810
[CHILD A]
I think this house
belongs to that pretty lady.

42
00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:50.980
The one who plays her harp
on the beach all the time.

43
00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.560
Yeah. You're right.
This is her house. For sure.

44
00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:55.720
Her name's Conis,

45
00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.100
and she lives here with
her dad, Pagaya.

46
00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.890
They both seem like
really nice people.

47
00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:03.570
They even invited me over
to have lunch one time.

48
00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:06.520
I heard that girl and her
dad are really bad people.

49
00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:10.150
Stay away or you'll
get in trouble.

50
00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:11.840
[CHILD C]
My mom told me that, too.

51
00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:16.130
She said that they were
helping the Blue Sea People.

52
00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:18.180
[gasps]
That can't be.

53
00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:20.220
I swear! It's true!
They're trouble!

54
00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:23.390
My father said he'd ground me if
he caught me anywhere near them!

55
00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.310
Your father said that... I see.

56
00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.830
Oh. I'm sorry, I just
remembered your father is...

57
00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:33.150
Heh... My daddy's
a member of the Enforcers,

58
00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.000
and he's out on patrol.

59
00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.480
My mom says he'll be
coming home soon.

60
00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.650
And I can't hardly wait, 'cause
I've never even seen his face.

61
00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:41.770
Oh, man.

62
00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.780
I think it is so
awesome your dad is

63
00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:45.910
one of the Divine Warriors.

64
00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:48.870
And I'm sure your dad will come
to home to see you real soon.

65
00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.040
[CHILD B]
Yeah.

66
00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:56.710
[horn blares]

67
00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:59.860
[MAN A]
Skypiea will be dropped
back into the Blue Sea world.

68
00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:01.990
This nation will
no longer exist!

69
00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.260
[CONIS]
I can't let
his death be in vain.

70
00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:07.890
I must tell the others.

71
00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:11.390
I have to warn them,
no matter what it takes.

72
00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.440
What just happened?

73
00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.440
Why did all these ruins
fall out of the sky?

74
00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.750
[ROBIN]
Swordsman!

75
00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:27.280
[ZORO]
This is not my day...

76
00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.850
[ROBIN]
Don't tell me you fell
down here with all of this.

77
00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:31.570
[ZORO grunts]

78
00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:33.320
Yeah, I did.

79
00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.160
And it almost killed me.

80
00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:36.360
[ROBIN]
I'm amazed it didn't.

81
00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:36.670
Are you sure you're all right?

82
00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:39.800
Yeah. Good to see ya, Robin.

83
00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.260
Where am I?
What is this place?

84
00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:45.190
[ROBIN]
It's the city of gold
we've been looking for.

85
00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.940
Did you find the treasure?

86
00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.950
I didn't. There's no evidence
that gold was ever here.

87
00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:08.780
[LUFFY, AISA screaming]

88
00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.040
[gasps]

89
00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:20.080
Wow! That was one crazy ride
if I do say so myself.

90
00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:22.170
I think I wanna go again.

91
00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:23.590
[AISA]
Are you stupid?!

92
00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.090
Why in the world did you hold
onto the waver's jet?

93
00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.200
[LUFFY laughing]
Sorry.

94
00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.160
[AISA]
Everyone else managed to escape.

95
00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.030
And we've been left behind
because of your stupidity.

96
00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.120
It's all your fault!

97
00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:35.120
[LUFFY]
Eh. Don't worry.

98
00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.370
[AISA]
Get us outta here!

99
00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.240
I've got an idea. Why don't
we make our way down

100
00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:40.910
to the back of the snake and
escape out its butthole?

101
00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:43.950
Think again jerk!
That's not gonna happen!

102
00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:48.810
[LUFFY]
Look. It's the horse.

103
00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.200
That's a bird!

104
00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:55.530
[NAMI]
Ow!

105
00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:58.290
Thanks, Mr. Weirdo.

106
00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:02.690
We just got lucky when
we landed on these clouds.

107
00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.460
[NAMI]
We left Luffy and Aisa behind.

108
00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:06.840
I hope they're okay.

109
00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.880
Pierre's gone to
fetch your friends.

110
00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:10.510
And when push comes to shove,

111
00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:13.370
he's a very reliable
bird or horse.

112
00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:16.500
Hey. Where did we end up?
What is this place?

113
00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:21.210
Well, to be perfectly honest,
I have no idea where we are,

114
00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:24.720
but it looks like we
fell through the clouds.

115
00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:26.510
Thank you very much.

116
00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.470
I've traveled all across
the Upper Yard in my lifetime,

117
00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:34.390
but I've never seen
this place before.

118
00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:36.230
[WYPER gasping]

119
00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:51.600
Could it be? Is this
really our homeland?

120
00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:10.780
[SHANDORIAN WARRIORS]
– Light the fire of Shandora!
– Light the fire of Shandora!

121
00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:14.330
In the name of the
Great Warrior Kalgara!

122
00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:17.070
Light the Fire of Shandora!

123
00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:21.280
[SHANDORIAN WARRIORS yelling]

124
00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:23.280
[SHANDORIAN WARRIORS]
– We're going back...
– We're going back...

125
00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:25.500
...to our Homeland!

126
00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:31.280
[WYPER]
I've finally found
what I've been looking for!

127
00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:35.330
The proud city that my
ancestors protected!

128
00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:37.680
[WYPER]
Shandora!

129
00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:49.970
[gasps]

130
00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:52.890
[NAMI]
I think the snake is
looking for something.

131
00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:56.510
Either that or Luffy's doing
something that's bothering it.

132
00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:04.900
Huh. That snake sure
is acting strangely.

133
00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:11.320
[gasps]
I think it's crying.

134
00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:14.480
[roars]

135
00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.240
What's the meaning of
this ridiculous outburst?

136
00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:21.700
Just what are you getting
yourself so worked up about?

137
00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:22.900
You've always been
an annoyance to me.

138
00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:25.150
[ENERU]
But no longer.

139
00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:28.780
El Thor!

140
00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:33.700
[NAMI gasps]

141
00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:34.540
Aisa!

142
00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:37.000
Oh, no Nami! She's dead!

143
00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:40.830
There's no way she
could have survived that!

144
00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:42.380
Robin and Zoro?

145
00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:44.300
When did you guys get here?

146
00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.980
[ZORO]
Wait, what are you doin' there?

147
00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.560
How'd you get outta
that snake's stomach?

148
00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:50.460
Phew, glad to see you're
all right, Navigator.

149
00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:52.220
Yeah, I think I'm all right,

150
00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:56.890
but I'm not so sure...
about... the others.

151
00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:58.760
Luffy was still in there.

152
00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:01.220
Wha...?! What was he
doing in there?

153
00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:04.440
I tried to get him out,
but he fell off the waver.

154
00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:06.900
[ZORO]
Uh! That brat is
nothing but a pain in the ass.

155
00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:08.770
Is he aware of how much
of a hassle he is?

156
00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:10.730
How am I supposed to know?!

157
00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:14.800
[WYPER]
Just one hit.

158
00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:16.350
That's all it took.

159
00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:18.230
Eneru destroyed him
when my bazooka

160
00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:20.400
couldn't even scratch the snake.

161
00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:24.490
And Aisa. I can only hope
she somehow survived.

162
00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:28.240
[growls]

163
00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:33.540
[ENERU]
Ball Cloud!

164
00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:38.500
Eneru!

165
00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:40.350
[ENERU laughs]
That's no way to treat your host

166
00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:42.520
now is it, Shandorian Warrior!

167
00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:45.600
I thought that you'd be happy.

168
00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:47.690
After all, it was I
who brought you here

169
00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:50.110
and returned you
to your homeland.

170
00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:51.030
[WYPER growls]

171
00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:52.530
[ENERU]
Don't get so worked up.

172
00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:54.570
There's time for that later.

173
00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:56.230
This is the beginning.

174
00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:58.780
You don't want the fun
to end so soon, do you?

175
00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:00.260
This is a game to you?

176
00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:01.620
Yes.

177
00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:03.830
And a truly petty game at that.

178
00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:06.960
For all of you will be
competing against each other

179
00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.620
for my entertainment.

180
00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:24.780
Well done. I'm happy so many
of you've made it this far.

181
00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:27.780
I extend my welcome
to you survivors.

182
00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:31.120
[ENERU laughing]

183
00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:35.870
[laughs]

184
00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:38.620
[ENERU]
And now the fun truly begins.

185
00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:41.130
This is a survival game
to see how many people

186
00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:44.300
out of an original 81,
including myself,

187
00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:47.720
are still standing after
three hours on this island.

188
00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:50.850
The last person left will
of course be the winner.

189
00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:53.970
Among you are a few participants
who entered late into the game,

190
00:11:54.050 --> 00:11:56.430
but I've decided to
allow them to stay.

191
00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:59.130
It will make it all
the more interesting.

192
00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:01.050
Now the five of us
will continue on

193
00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:03.420
in the final stage of the game.

194
00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:06.280
[NAMI]
Did he say five people?

195
00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:11.030
Zoro, Robin, Gan Fall,
Bazooka man, and Eneru.

196
00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:13.300
That's exactly five people.

197
00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:16.930
Phew. Good thing he hasn't
noticed that I'm here.

198
00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:21.790
[ENERU]
In just a few minutes
the three hours will be up.

199
00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:25.080
Which means that the six
people we have present here

200
00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:27.130
are one too many.

201
00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:28.970
[NAMI]
He knows I'm here.

202
00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:31.470
The one thing I know
is that God's prophecy

203
00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:35.310
will never falter,
because he is absolute.

204
00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:38.440
I'm curious to see how this
person is going to die.

205
00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.060
Will you all fight each other?

206
00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.770
Will you gang up on one
of the weaker ones?

207
00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:47.940
Of course, you could all resist
your fates and force me to pick.

208
00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:52.790
What do you want to do, Robin?

209
00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:54.830
I'm not going to kill anyone.

210
00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:55.880
I won't either.

211
00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:58.550
I won't compete
in your sick game.

212
00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:02.680
And I too refuse to take part.

213
00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:04.260
[yelps]

214
00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:06.430
Why do you gotta
drag me into this?!

215
00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:07.630
[gasps]

216
00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:15.310
[ALL]
– You're the only one dying today!
– You're the only one dying today!

217
00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:21.110
[ENERU laughing]

218
00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:23.920
[ENERU]
Insolent fools.

219
00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:27.780
[ENERU]
You dare to threaten me?

220
00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:34.940
Whoa. This guy's dangerous!

221
00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:37.780
[ENERU laughing]

222
00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.660
I must admit,
I'm quite impressed.

223
00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:43.620
But you have no idea
what you're up against.

224
00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:47.540
Even the four of you together
don't stand a chance against me.

225
00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:53.330
You cannot comprehend...

226
00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:57.800
...the extent of my powers
and what I'm truly capable of.

227
00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:02.300
[laughing]
Look at you.

228
00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:04.810
An elderly buffoon
wanting peace.

229
00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:07.910
A warrior who single mindedly
seeks his homeland.

230
00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:10.100
And thieves from the Blue Sea

231
00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:13.020
who are only concerned
with treasures.

232
00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:15.940
All of you, for one reason
or another, seek to save

233
00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:18.480
this wretched place
called Skypiea.

234
00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:22.110
But you cannot, because this
nation is fundamentally flawed.

235
00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:23.100
[GAN FALL growls]

236
00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:24.720
[GAN FALL]
I refuse to stand here

237
00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:26.390
and listen to such nonsense.

238
00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:30.810
Now tell me where
the Divine Warriors are!

239
00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:33.650
And what exactly is
your goal here today?

240
00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:35.620
Why, an ascension.

241
00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:36.950
My old friend.

242
00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:38.560
What do you mean?

243
00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:41.040
[ENERU]
I mean, when I ascend

244
00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:44.330
I will return to
my rightful place.

245
00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:46.460
[GAN FALL]
What's that?

246
00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:49.090
Are you saying that you're
leaving Skypiea?

247
00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:50.550
[ENERU]
That's right.

248
00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:53.820
I will soon leave this
dreadful wasteland.

249
00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:56.740
On the island where I grew up
there were legends of a place

250
00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:58.850
regarded as God's Home.

251
00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:00.370
As God's home?

252
00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:03.080
People call this place
Endless Vearth.

253
00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:05.750
And there... the ground
extends as far

254
00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:09.880
as the eye can see
in all directions.

255
00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:13.840
It's my dream to find
this place. This paradise!

256
00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:19.400
Endless Vearth.
A home fit for a God!

257
00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:22.920
My time spent here battling
over the inconsequential

258
00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:25.780
lands of the Upper Yard
has been nothing

259
00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.660
but a petty triviality.

260
00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:32.760
[ENERU]
Listen to me.

261
00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:37.020
I tell you this place that you
cherish is an abomination.

262
00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:39.940
Consider this...

263
00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:43.840
[ENERU]
It was born in the sky,
though it's not a cloud.

264
00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:46.760
It lives in the sky,
though it's not a bird.

265
00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:51.150
[ENERU]
This nation
which exists in the sky

266
00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.870
is an utterly unnatural one.

267
00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:57.740
When we die we all return
to the Earth, to the soil,

268
00:15:57.820 --> 00:16:01.240
but here... there is none.

269
00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:04.030
What exactly are you getting at?

270
00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:09.490
[ENERU]
You really shouldn't be
surprised by my intentions.

271
00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:16.330
As God, I'm bound to adhere to
the divine province on nature.

272
00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:20.040
That's why...
this unnatural nation...

273
00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:23.000
...will be ripped apart
and pulled from the sky!

274
00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:24.120
[gasping]

275
00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:26.380
[gasps]

276
00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:27.920
[growls]

277
00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:32.510
[GAN FALL]
You're planning on
wiping out Skypiea completely?

278
00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:34.880
[ENERU]
It's only natural.

279
00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:38.600
[GAN FALL]
Don't be so conceited.

280
00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:40.980
The term "God" is just
a title used to refer

281
00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:43.140
to the leader of this nation!

282
00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.860
True. But that will soon change.

283
00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:50.300
[GAN FALL]
A true God does
not live amongst the humans

284
00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:53.640
like you do and treat
them as his playthings!

285
00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:56.180
[ENERU]
Former God...

286
00:16:56.270 --> 00:17:00.230
Gan Fall. [laughs]

287
00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:04.230
You're worried about the
Divine Warriors, are you not?

288
00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:09.610
[ENERU]
Six years ago, your
Divine Warriors lost a battle

289
00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.310
against my forces and I took
650 of your subordinates

290
00:17:13.390 --> 00:17:15.220
under my charge.

291
00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:18.480
They served me well,
until this morning

292
00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:20.690
when I could find no
more use for them.

293
00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:23.520
I told you, did I not?

294
00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:27.190
The six of us here now
are the only ones left alive

295
00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.490
in this forsaken place.

296
00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.180
Such a shame.

297
00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:34.190
[GAN FALL]
You... monster...

298
00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:36.650
[ENERU]
It's not that I
wanted to harm them.

299
00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:40.650
But when I told them my goal,
they dared to challenge me.

300
00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:45.420
[laughing]
And they paid the
price for that insubordination.

301
00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:46.630
[laughing]

302
00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:52.210
They were good men, and they all
had families on Angel Island.

303
00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:53.890
[ENERU]
Yes, I'm aware.

304
00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:57.640
I supposed I'll have to bury
their families beside them.

305
00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:02.150
[GAN FALL]
You are...

306
00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:07.610
[GAN FALL]
...the devil!

307
00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:10.240
[GAN FALL yelling]

308
00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:25.130
[ENERU]
Five million...

309
00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:26.290
Ten million...

310
00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:28.630
Twenty million...

311
00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:31.880
[GAN FALL]
We were...

312
00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.140
[OHM]
Eneru.

313
00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:36.770
What should we do
with this old man?

314
00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:39.020
He's pathetic. He's useless.

315
00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:40.150
Can we kill him?

316
00:18:40.230 --> 00:18:42.020
[ENERU]
Just throw him into the sea.

317
00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:44.850
I doubt he can even be
used for manual labor.

318
00:18:46.630 --> 00:18:48.280
[ENERU laughs]
This shrine on the other hand

319
00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:49.780
could be quite useful to us.

320
00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:54.360
But what we really need are the
services of the Divine Warriors.

321
00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:58.660
They could be put to work in
bringing about my ultimate goal.

322
00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:01.750
They will never
help you in your cause.

323
00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:04.630
Silence. You're no longer
in charge, old man.

324
00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:06.180
[GAN FALL screams]

325
00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:09.390
[ENERU laughing]

326
00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:16.480
[ENERU]
Twenty million volts.

327
00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:19.270
[screams]

328
00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:21.460
[NAMI]
No, get away from him!

329
00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:22.580
[WYPER gasping]

330
00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:28.480
[ENERU]
God does exist in this world.

331
00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.620
[GAN FALL]
How mortifying.

332
00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:33.610
And that God is me.

333
00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:41.370
It's the devil fruit.

334
00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:43.440
It's the Rumble-Rumble Fruit.

335
00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:45.820
If I'm not mistaken,
this particular fruit

336
00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:48.740
is said to have the
power of invincibility.

337
00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:52.320
[ROBIN]
The power of lightning!

338
00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:55.280
[ROBIN]
The power of lightning!

339
00:19:55.280 --> 00:19:56.740
But... lightning.

340
00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:58.160
There's no way!

341
00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:01.200
A human has no
chance against that!

342
00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:05.420
[ENERU]
It is time.

343
00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:11.090
All that I have foreseen
will finally come to be.

344
00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.990
The four of you should
feel honored

345
00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:15.200
to have survived this long.

346
00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:17.610
[laughing]

347
00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:20.950
Now... Come along,
you will join me

348
00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:24.610
as I gain passage
to my dream world...

349
00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:26.670
...to the Endless Vearth!

350
00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:30.260
Come with me!
Come and fulfill your destinies.

351
00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:31.800
Why would we?

352
00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:35.250
[ENERU]
There I will build an
indisputable Nation of God!

353
00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:37.920
Where only the chosen ones
are permitted to live.

354
00:20:37.930 --> 00:20:41.930
A utopia of boundless
and eternal power.

355
00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:44.060
What is he saying?

356
00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:46.480
[ENERU]
I will not let those
who are unworthy,

357
00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:49.150
like those incompetent
subordinates of mine,

358
00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:51.860
sully the stature of
this new nation.

359
00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:54.530
Only those who pass
my judgment may bask

360
00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:55.940
in the glory of my company.

361
00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:56.950
[ROBIN]
But...

362
00:20:57.070 --> 00:20:59.870
And, what will you
do if we refuse?

363
00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:01.670
No. Robin.

364
00:21:01.670 --> 00:21:02.820
[ENERU]
Refuse?

365
00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:05.790
But why? Why refuse to join me?

366
00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:08.170
If you stay here you'll
fall into a bottomless pit

367
00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:10.400
along with the rest of
this unnatural nation.

368
00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:12.690
I have no doubt you could
destroy the entirety

369
00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:14.930
of the Upper Yard
in one fell swoop.

370
00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:17.800
But if you decide to
destroy all this,

371
00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:20.070
then won't you also be
destroying something

372
00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:22.620
that you cherish?

373
00:21:22.770 --> 00:21:24.390
Do you mean the Golden Bell?

374
00:21:24.710 --> 00:21:25.810
[ROBIN]
Yes, that's right.

375
00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:27.520
What's the Golden Bell?

376
00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:28.820
[WYPER growls]

377
00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:30.320
[ROBIN]
The Golden Bell.

378
00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:32.360
[ENERU laughs]

379
00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:34.570
Oh, don't worry. No need.

380
00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:37.330
I've already made arrangements.

381
00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:40.580
Based on what I know about
your travels across Skypiea,

382
00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:43.010
I believe I know where
the bell is located.

383
00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:46.510
[ENERU]
That's right.
I know what you're thinking.

384
00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:49.430
And it won't be long
before I have the bell.

385
00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:51.970
You seem surprised.

386
00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:54.680
Did you really think
that you, a mere human,

387
00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:58.020
could ever get the better of me?

388
00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.020
How foolish of you.

389
00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:02.340
[NAMI]
Robin!

390
00:22:02.570 --> 00:22:04.860
There's nothing I hate
more in this world

391
00:22:04.950 --> 00:22:07.740
than a cold, calculating woman.

392
00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:09.550
No...

393
00:22:09.630 --> 00:22:10.750
[WYPER growls]

394
00:22:10.840 --> 00:22:11.880
[grunts]

395
00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:34.390
[ZORO]
How dare you!

396
00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:35.730
Heh.

397
00:22:35.810 --> 00:22:37.860
I do as I please.

398
00:22:37.940 --> 00:22:39.230
[ZORO growls]

399
00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:54.230
You've got skills.

400
00:22:54.760 --> 00:22:56.980
And you are completely
out of your mind.

401
00:22:57.500 --> 00:22:59.130
[ZORO grunts]

402
00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:08.990
[WYPER]
Burn Bazooka!

403
00:23:10.930 --> 00:23:13.220
[ENERU chuckles]

404
00:23:13.310 --> 00:23:15.100
Kari!

405
00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:26.250
Uh. No way!

406
00:23:26.330 --> 00:23:29.130
How did he manage to neutralize
the bazooka's blast?

407
00:23:29.910 --> 00:23:32.560
[ENERU]
Hmph. You still
don't get it, do you?

408
00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:34.970
Your energy doesn't
even register to me.

409
00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:38.300
I'm more powerful than you
could ever comprehend.

410
00:23:38.390 --> 00:23:40.220
The thunderclap reverberated.

411
00:23:40.310 --> 00:23:42.140
And that only happens
when the air expands

412
00:23:42.220 --> 00:23:43.520
at the speed of sound.

413
00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:44.900
That's really powerful.

414
00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:48.670
That amount of power is greater
than anything we can handle.

415
00:23:48.730 --> 00:23:49.850
It's true...

416
00:23:49.930 --> 00:23:52.690
He really is made of lightning.

417
00:23:52.770 --> 00:23:54.060
[ENERU]
The time is near.

418
00:23:54.150 --> 00:23:55.940
Prepare yourselves.

419
00:23:56.030 --> 00:23:57.900
Soon those who
remain will set off

420
00:23:57.990 --> 00:23:59.820
for the Endless Vearth together.

421
00:23:59.900 --> 00:24:03.700
Do you even understand what
a rare privilege this is?

422
00:24:03.750 --> 00:24:06.790
And why do you assume
we'll come willingly?

423
00:24:06.870 --> 00:24:08.080
[ENERU]
Hm?

424
00:24:09.260 --> 00:24:11.010
[ZORO growling]

425
00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:15.180
[ZORO]
I don't give a damn about
your so called "dream world"!

426
00:24:16.380 --> 00:24:17.430
Zoro!

427
00:24:17.510 --> 00:24:19.760
Stay away from him!
He's too powerful!

428
00:24:19.850 --> 00:24:21.140
You need a lesson.

429
00:24:21.230 --> 00:24:23.440
Soon your body will know

430
00:24:23.520 --> 00:24:25.770
the power of God.

431
00:24:26.690 --> 00:24:30.990
[ZORO growling]

432
00:24:31.070 --> 00:24:33.320
[ZORO grunting]

433
00:24:38.350 --> 00:24:39.980
[ZORO]
Uh...!

434
00:24:40.060 --> 00:24:41.690
[ENERU]
I possess a tremendous power

435
00:24:41.770 --> 00:24:45.780
that you puny humans can
never hope to overcome.

436
00:24:45.860 --> 00:24:48.610
Can you feel it now?

437
00:24:48.700 --> 00:24:50.660
The despair?

438
00:24:55.870 --> 00:24:58.410
If one loses all hope
it is an experience

439
00:24:58.500 --> 00:25:00.790
not unlike losing one's life.

440
00:25:03.630 --> 00:25:05.510
[NAMI]
Zoro!

441
00:25:07.280 --> 00:25:10.700
[ENERU]
People fear death
above all things.

442
00:25:13.850 --> 00:25:15.980
[ENERU]
That's why people
prostrate themselves

443
00:25:16.060 --> 00:25:19.100
before an insurmountable
power and beg for mercy.

444
00:25:19.190 --> 00:25:21.520
It is simply the natural
order of things.

445
00:25:21.610 --> 00:25:24.320
Beings are meant to bow
before that which they fear.

446
00:25:24.400 --> 00:25:25.570
It's a shame.

447
00:25:25.650 --> 00:25:28.110
You are bound by your instincts.

448
00:25:28.200 --> 00:25:31.240
[ZORO]
Can't believe how
incredibly strong he is.

449
00:25:32.240 --> 00:25:33.490
[NAMI gasps]

450
00:25:37.870 --> 00:25:39.920
What do you think
you're trying to do?

451
00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:42.290
[panting]

452
00:25:42.380 --> 00:25:45.840
And now... time to die.

453
00:25:45.920 --> 00:25:51.180
[WYPER]
Are you familiar with
the Sea Prism Stone, Eneru?

454
00:25:51.260 --> 00:25:53.100
[ZORO]
Sea Prism Stone?

455
00:25:53.200 --> 00:25:57.290
That's a stone that can
counteract devil fruit powers.

456
00:26:01.920 --> 00:26:06.000
[ENERU]
Well then, do your
worst, Shandorian.

457
00:26:06.140 --> 00:26:07.350
Sea Prism Stone.

458
00:26:07.430 --> 00:26:08.720
It's said to harness the power

459
00:26:08.740 --> 00:26:11.950
of the entire ocean
into a single blast.

460
00:26:12.060 --> 00:26:14.560
It's the sea condensed
into solid form.

461
00:26:14.690 --> 00:26:16.900
If anything can overcome
the power of the devil fruit,

462
00:26:16.980 --> 00:26:18.610
it's the Stone.

463
00:26:18.680 --> 00:26:20.600
[WYPER]
Die!

464
00:26:20.680 --> 00:26:22.140
Are you sure you know
what you're doing?

465
00:26:22.190 --> 00:26:24.450
You're aware of the
consequences, are you not?

466
00:26:24.560 --> 00:26:27.690
Your body will pay a
heavy price, as well.

467
00:26:27.770 --> 00:26:31.150
Why sacrifice yourself for a
homeland you will never regain?

468
00:26:31.230 --> 00:26:35.820
If I must... I'll die. Glady...

469
00:26:35.900 --> 00:26:38.530
If it means I can
take you with me!

470
00:26:38.610 --> 00:26:39.450
[gasps]

471
00:26:39.530 --> 00:26:41.490
[ENERU]
Don't do it.

472
00:26:43.790 --> 00:26:45.040
Reject!

473
00:26:50.270 --> 00:26:52.320
[CHIEFTAIN]
Hold our true
ambitions in your heart

474
00:26:52.400 --> 00:26:54.070
and speak not of them.

475
00:26:54.150 --> 00:26:57.030
We are the weavers of history.

476
00:26:57.110 --> 00:26:59.070
Those are the words
that were written on

477
00:26:59.160 --> 00:27:03.240
a Poneglyph 800 years ago.

478
00:27:03.330 --> 00:27:04.830
[WYPER]
Poneglyph?

479
00:27:04.910 --> 00:27:08.210
[CHIEFTAIN]
Yes. And when those
who sought to steal the stone

480
00:27:08.290 --> 00:27:11.380
revealed themselves,
the Shandorian Warriors

481
00:27:11.460 --> 00:27:16.260
of the City of Gold fought
bravely to protect it.

482
00:27:16.350 --> 00:27:17.440
[WYPER]
Did they succeed?

483
00:27:18.120 --> 00:27:21.500
Yes. They did. However...

484
00:27:21.560 --> 00:27:23.430
...the battle took its toll.

485
00:27:23.540 --> 00:27:26.880
A great many warriors
died that day.

486
00:27:26.900 --> 00:27:30.460
Those few who survived vowed to
become guardians of the stone.

487
00:27:30.710 --> 00:27:33.760
They kept watch over the city
and the sacred Poneglyph

488
00:27:33.840 --> 00:27:36.720
they swore to
defend to the death.

489
00:27:36.780 --> 00:27:41.410
[WYPER]
And you say that's the
true story of our ancestors?

490
00:27:41.500 --> 00:27:43.920
But then the island and City
of Gold were taken away

491
00:27:44.000 --> 00:27:46.540
to Skypiea 400 years ago.

492
00:27:46.620 --> 00:27:49.540
Since then, it's been
under Skypiean control.

493
00:27:49.620 --> 00:27:51.290
[WYPER]
Our ancestors
fought to their last breath

494
00:27:51.370 --> 00:27:52.500
to defend that island.

495
00:27:52.800 --> 00:27:53.740
And then it was taken away!

496
00:27:56.790 --> 00:27:58.710
The Upper Yard.

497
00:27:58.800 --> 00:28:01.460
That is our homeland,
but at the same time,

498
00:28:01.550 --> 00:28:04.130
it alone holds a history
that has disappeared

499
00:28:04.220 --> 00:28:06.390
into the darkness of time.

500
00:28:06.470 --> 00:28:09.470
Even though it's is under the
control of the Skypieans now,

501
00:28:09.560 --> 00:28:13.060
we must never allow the fire
of the proud city of Shandora

502
00:28:13.140 --> 00:28:14.520
to die out.

503
00:28:14.600 --> 00:28:17.620
[WYPER breathes heavily]

504
00:28:17.620 --> 00:28:20.630
Oh no...

505
00:28:20.630 --> 00:28:23.220
[NAMI]
No way...

506
00:28:23.300 --> 00:28:25.260
He really did it.

507
00:28:50.120 --> 00:28:51.870
[NAMI]
It can't be.

508
00:28:53.870 --> 00:28:56.290
[NAMI]
He's restarting his own heart!

509
00:29:03.380 --> 00:29:05.840
[groans]

510
00:29:14.060 --> 00:29:17.060
[ENERU]
It's not that people fear God.

511
00:29:19.310 --> 00:29:22.530
Rather, it is God
who is fear itself.

512
00:29:26.280 --> 00:29:29.050
[ZORO]
What the hell is with this guy?

513
00:29:29.120 --> 00:29:31.330
[chuckles]

514
00:29:31.410 --> 00:29:35.000
[ENERU]
Wyper. I warned you, did I not?

515
00:29:36.080 --> 00:29:38.620
I warned you of
the consequences.

516
00:29:38.710 --> 00:29:40.420
[WYPER grunts]

517
00:29:40.500 --> 00:29:42.250
[WYPER groans]

518
00:29:42.340 --> 00:29:44.460
[ENERU]
And now look where you are.

519
00:29:46.370 --> 00:29:48.580
[ENERU]
How pitiful.

520
00:29:49.730 --> 00:29:52.400
[ENERU]
You call yourself a warrior?

521
00:29:54.610 --> 00:29:55.820
[WYPER]
Don't address me...

522
00:29:55.900 --> 00:29:57.440
[ENERU]

523
00:29:57.530 --> 00:30:00.400
...as if you know
anything about me!

524
00:30:01.220 --> 00:30:03.200
[WYPER]
Eight hundred years ago,

525
00:30:04.310 --> 00:30:08.360
proud Shandorian warriors fought
for the fate of this city.

526
00:30:08.440 --> 00:30:11.360
They fought to their
death to protect it.

527
00:30:11.440 --> 00:30:15.280
I am a descendant
of those warriors.

528
00:30:15.360 --> 00:30:18.570
One day, our homeland
was taken away from us.

529
00:30:18.680 --> 00:30:21.930
For 400 years we've carried
The Great Warrior Kalgara's

530
00:30:22.010 --> 00:30:23.310
injured pride.

531
00:30:23.390 --> 00:30:25.350
We've sought to return
our homeland to its

532
00:30:25.430 --> 00:30:27.730
rightful place for generations.

533
00:30:27.810 --> 00:30:29.110
And now that...

534
00:30:29.210 --> 00:30:31.580
...I've finally made it...

535
00:30:36.960 --> 00:30:38.670
...you're standing...

536
00:30:38.760 --> 00:30:42.640
...in... my... way.

537
00:30:48.230 --> 00:30:50.770
[ENERU]
I must admit
you landed a good blow.

538
00:30:52.500 --> 00:30:56.330
But what a cheap trick,
using that Sea Prism Stone.

539
00:30:56.420 --> 00:30:58.210
And on top of that,

540
00:30:58.280 --> 00:31:01.780
using a Reject dial should
easily kill the ordinary user.

541
00:31:01.870 --> 00:31:05.460
But you shot it twice and
you're still breathing.

542
00:31:05.540 --> 00:31:08.500
[ENERU scoffs]
Quite impressive.

543
00:31:09.630 --> 00:31:12.090
[grunts]

544
00:31:12.170 --> 00:31:15.920
[ENERU]
However, you're still
no match for me.

545
00:31:18.090 --> 00:31:20.510
[gasps]

546
00:31:22.670 --> 00:31:25.510
Is that... a bird?

547
00:31:28.980 --> 00:31:31.730
[ENERU]
Thirty million volt Hino.

548
00:31:33.110 --> 00:31:34.320
[ENERU grunts]

549
00:31:36.360 --> 00:31:38.240
[WYPER gasps, shouts]

550
00:31:40.620 --> 00:31:45.330
[yells]

551
00:31:47.290 --> 00:31:48.750
[ZORO grunts]

552
00:31:48.780 --> 00:31:52.660
[ZORO]
So this has a Sea
Prism Stone in it, huh?

553
00:31:52.870 --> 00:31:56.200
And now it's your turn,
Swordsman of the Blue Sea.

554
00:31:56.880 --> 00:32:00.050
The only choice now is
to kill or be killed!

555
00:32:01.970 --> 00:32:03.180
[ENERU]
Kiten!

556
00:32:05.350 --> 00:32:08.640
[ZORO grunts, shouts]

557
00:32:08.720 --> 00:32:11.730
[ZORO yells]

558
00:32:11.820 --> 00:32:12.790
Zoro!

559
00:32:27.060 --> 00:32:29.050
[NAMI]
I don't believe it!

560
00:32:29.890 --> 00:32:31.260
Even Zoro!

561
00:32:32.170 --> 00:32:35.460
[NAMI]
Everyone... has fallen to him.

562
00:32:43.680 --> 00:32:45.310
[gasps]

563
00:32:45.390 --> 00:32:47.230
How could he?

564
00:32:55.610 --> 00:32:57.530
[NAMI]
Unreal.

565
00:32:58.530 --> 00:33:00.950
[NAMI]
Even as hurt as he is...

566
00:33:02.840 --> 00:33:04.810
[NAMI]
...he still intends to fight.

567
00:33:07.560 --> 00:33:09.520
[ENERU]
What do you hope to prove?

568
00:33:09.540 --> 00:33:10.960
You're going to die anyway.

569
00:33:11.040 --> 00:33:13.670
Why not make it
easy on yourself?

570
00:33:15.840 --> 00:33:18.430
Did you say it's been 400 years?

571
00:33:18.520 --> 00:33:21.320
For all that time you and the
Shandorians have been fighting

572
00:33:21.400 --> 00:33:23.320
to take back your homeland?

573
00:33:23.410 --> 00:33:25.950
And yet, you are the only
warrior who was managed

574
00:33:26.040 --> 00:33:29.000
to make it here. No wonder
this nation will soon fall

575
00:33:29.080 --> 00:33:31.790
to the Blue Sea and be
lost for all eternity.

576
00:33:31.880 --> 00:33:33.590
[NAMI]
How could he do that?

577
00:33:35.420 --> 00:33:37.800
[ENERU]
You're fighting
for a lost cause.

578
00:33:37.860 --> 00:33:40.620
Can't you see that you'll never
regain your homeland?

579
00:33:40.700 --> 00:33:41.990
[NAMI]
He's unstoppable!

580
00:33:42.080 --> 00:33:44.450
[ENERU]
So why get back up?

581
00:33:47.880 --> 00:33:49.880
For my ancestors.

582
00:33:56.560 --> 00:34:00.020
I must confess I was hoping for
a better answer than that.

583
00:34:00.300 --> 00:34:03.400
But then again, I doubt you're
even completely conscious.

584
00:34:07.570 --> 00:34:09.070
[gasps]

585
00:34:11.040 --> 00:34:12.740
[NAMI]
Look out!

586
00:34:12.740 --> 00:34:15.080
Wyper, come here.

587
00:34:17.380 --> 00:34:18.080
[WYPER]
What is it?

588
00:34:22.220 --> 00:34:23.890
[CHIEFTAIN]
Since you
are a descendent of the

589
00:34:23.970 --> 00:34:28.310
Great Warrior Kalgara, I feel
I must impart this to you.

590
00:34:28.390 --> 00:34:31.650
Not many know the real reason
Kalgara wanted to regain

591
00:34:31.730 --> 00:34:35.070
the homeland, and why he would
stop at nothing to do so.

592
00:34:35.150 --> 00:34:38.610
[WYPER]
So tell me.
What's the real reason?

593
00:34:38.700 --> 00:34:42.240
[CHIEFTAIN]
You see. Kalgara
felt that the loss of his

594
00:34:42.320 --> 00:34:45.160
homeland was his
greatest failure.

595
00:34:45.240 --> 00:34:50.210
The problem was, he lost
something else important to him.

596
00:34:52.170 --> 00:34:54.000
[footsteps]

597
00:35:16.690 --> 00:35:20.100
[ENERU]
Of all who stood before
me, you are the only one left.

598
00:35:23.490 --> 00:35:24.910
[gasps]

599
00:35:32.750 --> 00:35:34.840
[gasps]

600
00:35:42.390 --> 00:35:45.640
[NAMI]
I... Just hear me out.

601
00:35:46.930 --> 00:35:49.100
[NAMI whimpers]

602
00:35:50.290 --> 00:35:53.210
[NAMI]
I want to...
I want to go with you.

603
00:35:59.450 --> 00:36:02.370
I've always wanted to
go to Endless Vearth.

604
00:36:02.680 --> 00:36:04.310
To your dream world.

605
00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:11.210
Can I come with you?
